       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. At that level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intended, and I'll enter it. If you confirm the original dose, I'd add a note to the order that it exceeds the usual maximum."
      }
